normally|usual-circumstances|ADVERB|In usual circumstances|In the way or at the time that is usual.|thường; thông thường|The gallery normally opens at ten, but today it opens later.|Phòng trưng bày thường mở lúc mười giờ, nhưng hôm nay mở muộn hơn.|Often before a main verb or after be; contrasts the usual pattern with an exception.|0
normally|in-a-normal-way|ADVERB|In a normal way|In the expected or usual manner, without an unusual problem.|bình thường|After the repair, the sliding door moved normally again.|Sau khi sửa, cánh cửa trượt lại di chuyển bình thường.|Often follows an action verb; function normally, breathe normally. Normal is the adjective.|1
south|southern-direction-or-region|NOUN|Southern direction or region|The direction opposite north, or the part of a place in that direction.|phía nam; miền nam|The storm moved towards the south during the evening.|Cơn bão di chuyển về phía nam trong buổi tối.|Usually the south; in the south of a country. Proper regional names may use a capital.|0
south|on-the-southern-side|ADJECTIVE|On the southern side|Located on or facing the side towards the south.|ở phía nam; hướng nam|Sunlight entered through the south window.|Ánh nắng chiếu vào qua cửa sổ hướng nam.|Before a noun; the south coast, a south-facing window. Southern is a related adjective.|1
south|towards-the-south|ADVERB|Towards the south|In the direction of south.|về phía nam|The hikers turned south at the stone bridge.|Những người đi bộ đường dài rẽ về phía nam tại cây cầu đá.|Go south, head south; no to is needed before this adverb.|2
weave|interlace-material|VERB|Interlace material|To make fabric or another object by passing threads or strips over and under each other.|dệt; đan|They weave baskets from thin strips of bamboo.|Họ đan giỏ bằng những nan tre mỏng.|Weave, wove, woven in this making sense; weave cloth, weave something from material.|0
weave|move-in-a-winding-route|VERB|Move in a winding route|To move along a route that repeatedly bends around obstacles.|luồn lách; đi ngoằn ngoèo|The cyclist weaved between the cones on the practice course.|Người đi xe đạp luồn lách giữa các cọc tiêu trên đường tập.|Weaved is usual for the movement sense; weave through or between things. Wove is common in the fabric-making sense.|1
cookie|small-sweet-baked-food|NOUN|Small sweet baked food|A small, usually sweet baked food that is often flat and round.|bánh quy|The children shared a plate of oatmeal cookies.|Những đứa trẻ chia nhau một đĩa bánh quy yến mạch.|Countable; cookie is especially American English. Biscuit is usual for many comparable foods in British English.|0
forward|towards-the-front|ADVERB|Towards the front|Towards the front or in the direction one is facing.|về phía trước|Please step forward when your number is called.|Hãy bước về phía trước khi số của bạn được gọi.|Move forward, look forward; forwards is also an adverb, especially in British English.|0
forward|at-or-towards-the-front|ADJECTIVE|At or towards the front|Situated nearer the front or directed towards it.|ở phía trước; hướng về phía trước|Passengers in the forward section left through the front door.|Hành khách ở khu vực phía trước ra bằng cửa trước.|Before a noun: forward section, forward movement. This does not cover the interpersonal boldness sense.|1
